WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.000
"Avatar 2" plunges moviegoers back into the
beautifully-realized world of Pandora, but

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.219
did James Cameron forget to flesh out the
film's heroine?

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:11.820
Neytiri, we hardly know you.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.929
In terms of its visuals, 2009's "Avatar" remains
in a class all its own.

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:20.670
It revolutionized 3D in Hollywood for several
years, to the point where you practically

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:25.289
couldn't see any movie in a theater without
it getting a rushed 3D treatment.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:30.170
When it comes to criticizing "Avatar," most
people take issue with the story itself.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.850
Drawing comparisons to "FernGully: The Last
Rainforest" and "Pocahontas," "Avatar" has

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:41.025
your typical white savior story of a marine,
Jake Sully, who's given a new body via an avatar.

00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:46.000
He then assimilates into Na'vi culture, and
while he was initially on the side of humanity,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.140
he soon switches over to the indigenous Na'vi,
realizing they shouldn't have their way of

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.710
life upended due to colonization.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.630
And who helps him along that journey but his
soon-to-be wife, Neytiri.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:00.960
Neytiri may be a secondary protagonist, but
in "Avatar," she has a worthwhile arc all

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.960
her own.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.420
She brings Jake into her tribe, but turns
her back on him once she realizes he was acting

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.000
as a spy the whole time.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.330
After he proves his intentions are pure, she
comes back around and falls in love with him

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.440
all over again.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.090
Her character arc is one of acceptance and
willingness to trust.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.250
It's just a shame she isn't given more to
do in the latest installment of the franchise

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.470
— "Avatar: The Way of Water."

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:28.400
Neytiri is a fierce warrior — that much
is evident from the film's opening sequences.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.990
Whether hunting for food for her family or
taking down a supply chain from the Sky People,

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.710
Neytiri has the skill and bravery to get the
job done.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:40.649
It's just a shame we never really get a chance
to see her put her skills in action more in

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:41.649
"The Way of Water."

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:45.689
After Jake and Neytiri's children are put
in harm's way by the resurrected avatar body

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:50.780
of Colonel Quaritch, Jake realizes that he
can't endanger his loved ones over this war.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.210
As a result, they decide to move away to be
with another clan while someone else takes

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.310
Jake's place.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:00.680
Neytiri's against it, but eventually, she
relents and agrees to go for the betterment

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.680
of her family.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.414
"I need you with me."

00:02:04.414 --> 00:02:07.280
From that point forward, Neytiri remains stagnant.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.250
She loves her family, and it's clear she would
do anything to keep them safe.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.319
She also wants to be a warrior, but there's
too much story going on for everyone else,

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:19.940
where it feels like Neytiri gets pushed to
the side to do anything interesting with either

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.310
of those ideas.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:26.120
In "The Way of Water," Neytiri pretty much
exists to react to her kids in peril, forfeiting

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.824
any potential for growth and instead being
relegated to a series of reactions.

00:02:30.824 --> 00:02:32.284
"This is our home!"

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:36.980
One reason why it feels Neytiri is so thinly
written could probably be attributed to there

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.800
being an abundance of characters for "The
Way of Water" to focus on.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.750
In addition to bringing back Jake and Neytiri,
they now have four children to care for.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:50.780
This is in addition to Spider, who has a tendency
to follow the family around in whatever they do.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:54.450
And that's not even getting into the new members
of the Metkayina clan.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:59.019
There's simply too much going on, and other
new characters get a chance at the limelight,

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:00.340
forcing Neytiri into the shadows.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:05.129
It's a shame, because there's something potentially
interesting about Neytiri wanting to juggle

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.219
her desire to be a warrior while protecting
her family.

00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:12.400
Based on recent reports, James Cameron has
an entire script of Jake and Neytiri's time

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.390
as warriors, which at least sounds like something
that would give Neytiri the development she

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.209
so desperately deserves.

00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:22.450
But the movie we got completely sidelines
her, to the point we don't even see her for

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.040
vast stretches of time.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.310
By the end of the film, we know just as much
about Neytiri as at the beginning of the film.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.610
She loves her family, and she'll kill to protect
them.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.739
But there's no forward growth.

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:37.600
Then again, if Cameron manages to get up to
"Avatar 7," there will be ample opportunities

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.379
to give Neytiri the character arc she deserves.

